WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
Two students.

2
00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.990
The same talk, word for word.

3
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:07.010
One speaks to the floor,
at one steady speed,

4
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.090
without a single pause.

5
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.980
The other looks up, and changes pace.

6
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.560
Same words, different result.

7
00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.240
So what changes besides the words?

8
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.260
In this mission, you'll
test the easy answers.

9
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.940
Is it a posher accent?

10
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.080
Is it just talking for longer?

11
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.460
You'll find out what spoken
Standard English really means,

12
00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.230
and sort lines from students' talks.

13
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.770
And you'll pick the rehearsal note
that would most improve a flat talk.

14
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.700
Your mission: find out what
changes besides the words.
